// PLAY-05 example — R2RML-classic Northwind subset.
//
// Demonstrates a relational-style "Customers" table → typed
// `ex:Customer` resources. This is the canonical R2RML/RML benchmark shape
// (one row → one resource, FK columns become resource IRIs).
//
// For the v0.1 demo we ship the Customers half — Orders + the FK join lives
// in the multi-source-join example so each example stays under 30 lines and
// teaches one idea well.

prefix ex:  <https://example.org/ecommerce/>
prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

buyers := io.csv("@examples/ecommerce-buyers.csv")

Customer : ex:Customer from buyers
    iri = `${ex:}customer/${.customer_id}`
    ex:name  = .name
    ex:email = .email
